@page "/institutions"
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components
@inject NavigationManager Navigation
<PageTitle>Development Briefing // The Singularity Workshop</PageTitle>

<div class="institution-brief">
    <header class="brief-signal"><span></span> THE SINGULARITY WORKSHOP <i>/ DEVELOPMENT BRIEFING</i></header>
    <main class="brief-layout stage-@_stage">
        <section class="brief-message">
            <div class="brief-kicker">FOR BRAVE1 · RESEARCH PROGRAMS · TECHNICAL PARTNERS</div>
            <div class="brief-stage">@(_stage switch { 0 => "01 / CENTRALIZE BEHAVIOR", 1 => "02 / TAKE IT INTO UNITY", 2 => "03 / BUILD THE ECOSYSTEM", _ => "04 / PROVE THE NEXT LEVEL" })</div>
            <div class="brief-scene" @key="_stage">
            @if (_stage == 0)
            {
                <h1>Behavior.<br/><em>One fluent API.</em></h1>
                <p class="brief-lede">I began with FSM_API: centralizing state behind a fluent, consistent API. Instead of scattering behavior across ad-hoc flags and conditionals, state transitions become explicit structures that can be inspected, tested, and changed at runtime.</p>
                <div class="brief-claim"><b>THE FIRST MILESTONE</b><span>A reusable .NET foundation, published independently of a game engine or user interface. The point wasn't a single demo; it was a common way to describe and govern behavior.</span></div>
                <div class="trl-readout"><small>DEVELOPMENT MATURITY / AUTHOR'S ESTIMATE</small><strong>TRL 5</strong><span>Foundation demonstrated in a relevant environment — an estimate to validate against formal TRL criteria.</span></div>
            }
            else if (_stage == 1)
            {
                <h1>Then, into<br/><em>Unity.</em></h1>
                <p class="brief-lede">Next came the Unity integration package. The foundation moved into a real-time engine context, then the work expanded across additional hosts and UI environments, including Blazor and WPF experiments.</p>
                <div class="brief-claim"><b>WHY THE INTEGRATION MATTERED</b><span>It tested the idea beyond an isolated library: a shared behavior model could support a practical application environment without making Unity types part of the portable core.</span></div>
                <div class="trl-readout"><small>DEVELOPMENT MATURITY / AUTHOR'S ESTIMATE</small><strong>TRL 6–7</strong><span>Estimated from demonstrations and integration breadth; independent assessment and evidence mapping remain necessary.</span></div>
            }
            else if (_stage == 2)
            {
                <h1>Now, the<br/><em>ecosystem.</em></h1>
                <p class="brief-lede">I'm building beyond the original FSM_API: FSM_Layer, MicroBundleDomain, FSM_COS, serialization, user I/O, GUI components, and manifest-driven WebPage/AnyApp experiences. The aim is to compose capabilities instead of rebuilding each application from scratch.</p>
                <div class="brief-claim"><b>THE CURRENT ENGINEERING CHALLENGE</b><span>Harden the composition path, make the experience reliable, measure the real behavior, and turn separate working parts into a repeatable end-to-end system.</span></div>
                <div class="trl-readout"><small>DEVELOPMENT MATURITY / AUTHOR'S ESTIMATE</small><strong>TRL 7–8</strong><span>Aspirational estimate for selected integrated demonstrations—not a claim that the ecosystem as a whole has been formally validated at that level.</span></div>
            }
            else
            {
                <h1>Demonstrate.<br/><em>Harden. Validate.</em></h1>
                <p class="brief-lede">The next step is not to declare military readiness. It is to make the WebPage experience solid, document evidence, define a real operational problem, and test against that problem's requirements. A future drone simulation—potentially 100,000 block-built agents—would be a demanding demonstration, not a substitute for validation.</p>
                <div class="brief-claim"><b>WHAT A PARTNER CAN HELP PROVE</b><span>Reliability, performance at stated scale, failure behavior, security boundaries, deployment repeatability, and mission-specific suitability. Each claim needs its own reproducible evidence.</span></div>
                <div class="trl-readout"><small>NEXT GATE</small><strong>Evidence first</strong><span>Agree on a use case, acceptance criteria, test environment, and measurable exit conditions before assigning a formal TRL.</span></div>
            }
            </div>
            <nav class="brief-steps" aria-label="Briefing sections">
                <button class="@(_stage == 0 ? "active" : "")" aria-pressed="@(_stage == 0)" @onclick="() => SetStage(0)">FOUNDATION</button>
                <button class="@(_stage == 1 ? "active" : "")" aria-pressed="@(_stage == 1)" @onclick="() => SetStage(1)">EVOLUTION</button>
                <button class="@(_stage == 2 ? "active" : "")" aria-pressed="@(_stage == 2)" @onclick="() => SetStage(2)">ECOSYSTEM</button>
                <button class="@(_stage == 3 ? "active" : "")" aria-pressed="@(_stage == 3)" @onclick="() => SetStage(3)">NEXT GATE</button>
            </nav>
            <div class="brief-actions">
                <button @onclick="RequestBriefing">DISCUSS A REAL PROBLEM <b>↗</b></button>
                <a href="https://github.com/TrentBest" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">INSPECT SOURCE & RELEASES ↗</a>
            </div>
        </section>
        <section class="brief-system" aria-label="Workshop architecture and development evidence">
            <div class="system-heading"><span>THE STACK</span><span>FOUNDATION → HOST</span></div>
            <div class="system-node node-domain"><small>WHAT / CAPABILITY IDENTITY</small><b>MicroBundleDomain</b><span>Ontology and capability contracts</span></div>
            <div class="system-link">↓</div>
            <div class="system-node node-fsm"><small>BEHAVIOR / PUBLISHED PACKAGE</small><b>FSM_API</b><span>Explicit state transitions · runtime change</span></div>
            <div class="system-link">↓</div>
            <div class="system-node node-layer"><small>ABSTRACTION</small><b>FSM_Layer</b><span>Higher-level state-machine organization</span></div>
            <div class="system-link">↓</div>
            <div class="system-node node-cos"><small>COMPOSITION / ACTIVE DEVELOPMENT</small><b>FSM_COS</b><span>Manifest-driven capability assembly</span></div>
            <div class="system-link">↓</div>
            <div class="system-node node-host"><small>EXPERIENCE / INTEGRATION TARGET</small><b>.NET host applications</b><span>Web · desktop · simulation · domain-specific systems</span></div>
            <div class="system-foot">EVIDENCE FIRST: SOURCE · TESTS · BENCHMARKS · INTEGRATION VALIDATION</div>
        </section>
    </main>
    <footer class="brief-footer"><span>DEVELOPMENT STATUS, NOT A PROCUREMENT CLAIM.</span><span>Scope and maturity are discussed openly.</span></footer>
</div>

<style>
.brief-scene{animation:briefSceneIn .65s cubic-bezier(.16,1,.3,1) both;transform-origin:left center}@@keyframes briefSceneIn{from{opacity:0;transform:translateY(10px) scale(.99);filter:blur(5px)}to{opacity:1;transform:translateY(0) scale(1);filter:blur(0)}}.trl-readout{display:grid;grid-template-columns:auto auto;align-items:center;gap:.25rem .8rem;margin-top:.65rem;padding:.6rem .75rem;border:1px solid #244657;background:linear-gradient(100deg,#00eaff0c,#ff2cff08);max-width:610px}.trl-readout small{grid-column:1/-1;color:#7fa6b5;font:700 .48rem Consolas,monospace;letter-spacing:.1em}.trl-readout strong{font:900 clamp(1.15rem,2vw,1.6rem) Consolas,monospace;color:var(--cyan);text-shadow:0 0 16px #00eaff35}.trl-readout span{font-size:.62rem;line-height:1.35;color:#9eb7c3}.brief-system .system-node{transition:opacity .5s ease,transform .5s ease,border-color .5s ease}.brief-system.stage-0 .node-fsm,.brief-system.stage-1 .node-fsm,.brief-system.stage-1 .node-host,.brief-system.stage-2 .node-cos,.brief-system.stage-2 .node-host,.brief-system.stage-3 .node-cos{border-color:var(--cyan);box-shadow:0 0 18px #00eaff12}.brief-system.stage-3 .system-foot{color:var(--cyan)}@media(max-width:620px){.trl-readout{padding:.4rem .5rem;gap:.2rem .5rem;margin-top:.35rem}.trl-readout span{font-size:.52rem}.trl-readout strong{font-size:1rem}.brief-scene{animation-duration:.45s}}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.brief-scene{animation:none}}.institution-brief{--cyan:#00eaff;--pink:#ff2cff;--gold:#ffd34d;position:relative;isolation:isolate;width:100%;height:100%;min-height:0;overflow:hidden;box-sizing:border-box;padding:clamp(.65rem,2vh,1.4rem) clamp(.8rem,2.5vw,2.4rem);background:radial-gradient(ellipse at 15% 35%,#092337 0,transparent 42%),radial-gradient(ellipse at 85% 65%,#210c2c 0,transparent 35%),#020711;color:#eaf8ff;font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;display:grid;grid-template-rows:auto minmax(0,1fr) auto;gap:clamp(.45rem,1.3vh,1rem)}
.brief-signal,.brief-kicker,.brief-stage,.system-heading,.system-node small,.system-link,.system-foot,.brief-footer,.brief-steps button{font-family:Consolas,monospace;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.1em}.brief-signal{font-size:.6rem;color:#a6c0cc;display:flex;gap:.65rem;align-items:center}.brief-signal>span{width:.48rem;height:.48rem;border-radius:50%;background:var(--cyan);box-shadow:0 0 12px var(--cyan)}.brief-signal i{font-style:normal;color:var(--pink)}
.brief-layout{min-height:0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(280px,.8fr);gap:clamp(1rem,3vw,3rem);align-items:center;max-width:1450px;width:100%;margin:auto}.brief-message{min-width:0}.brief-kicker{color:#80a9bb;font-size:.6rem;line-height:1.5}.brief-stage{color:var(--gold);font-size:.65rem;margin-top:.8rem}.brief-message h1{font-size:clamp(2.5rem,5.5vw,5.5rem);line-height:.9;letter-spacing:-.065em;margin:.65rem 0 1rem}.brief-message h1 em{font-style:normal;color:var(--cyan);text-shadow:0 0 35px #00eaff30}.brief-lede{max-width:60ch;font-size:clamp(.8rem,1.05vw,.98rem);line-height:1.62;color:#b3c8d2;margin:.5rem 0}.brief-claim{display:grid;gap:.4rem;margin-top:.85rem;padding:.8rem .9rem;border-left:2px solid var(--pink);background:#ff2cff0a;max-width:610px}.brief-claim b{font-size:.62rem;color:#ffadff}.brief-claim span{font-size:.8rem;line-height:1.5;color:#c3d2da}.brief-steps{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.4rem;margin-top:1rem}.brief-steps button{padding:.55rem .65rem;font-size:.58rem;color:#8aa9b6;background:#06121e;border:1px solid #244657;cursor:pointer}.brief-steps button.active{color:#061019;background:var(--cyan);border-color:var(--cyan)}.brief-actions{display:flex;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.6rem;margin-top:.8rem}.brief-actions button,.brief-actions a{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:.6rem;padding:.7rem .8rem;border:1px solid #00eaff70;background:#00eaff0b;color:#eaf8ff;text-decoration:none;font:800 .6rem Consolas,monospace;letter-spacing:.035em;cursor:pointer}.brief-actions button{background:var(--cyan);color:#031019;border-color:var(--cyan)}.brief-actions a:hover{border-color:var(--pink)}
.brief-system{min-width:0;padding:clamp(.7rem,1.5vw,1.2rem);border:1px solid #1b4558;background:linear-gradient(145deg,#071522ed,#030711f2);box-shadow:0 20px 70px #0005}.system-heading{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;color:#7198a9;margin-bottom:.65rem;font-size:.58rem}.system-node{display:grid;gap:.25rem;padding:.55rem .75rem;border:1px solid #244657;background:#05101b}.system-node small{font-size:.5rem;color:#7ea4b4}.system-node b{font:800 clamp(.78rem,1.1vw,.95rem) Consolas,monospace}.system-node span{font-size:.68rem;line-height:1.35;color:#9eb7c3}.node-domain{border-left:3px solid var(--gold)}.node-fsm{border-left:3px solid var(--cyan)}.node-layer{border-left:3px solid #a78bfa}.node-cos{border-left:3px solid var(--pink)}.node-host{border-left:3px solid #52e05a}.system-link{text-align:center;color:#638c9d;font-size:.55rem;padding:.17rem}.system-foot{border-top:1px solid #1b3544;margin-top:.6rem;padding-top:.6rem;color:#ffd34d;font-size:.49rem;line-height:1.45}.brief-footer{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:1rem;color:#648493;font-size:.5rem;line-height:1.4}
@@media(max-width:800px){.brief-layout{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(250px,.8fr);gap:.8rem}.brief-message h1{font-size:clamp(2.2rem,5.5vw,3.8rem)}.brief-system{padding:.65rem}.system-node{padding:.42rem .55rem}.system-node span{font-size:.61rem}}
@@media(max-width:620px){.institution-brief{height:100%;padding:.65rem;gap:.45rem}.brief-layout{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:.55rem;align-content:center}.brief-stage{margin-top:.4rem;font-size:.55rem}.brief-message h1{font-size:clamp(2rem,8vw,3rem);margin:.45rem 0}.brief-kicker{font-size:.5rem}.brief-lede{font-size:.7rem;line-height:1.35;margin:.35rem 0}.brief-claim{margin-top:.45rem;padding:.45rem .6rem;gap:.25rem}.brief-claim b{font-size:.52rem}.brief-claim span{font-size:.64rem;line-height:1.35}.brief-steps{margin-top:.5rem;gap:.3rem}.brief-steps button{font-size:.5rem;padding:.45rem}.brief-actions{margin-top:.5rem;gap:.35rem}.brief-actions button,.brief-actions a{font-size:.49rem;padding:.5rem}.brief-system{padding:.5rem}.system-heading{margin-bottom:.3rem;font-size:.48rem}.system-node{padding:.3rem .45rem;gap:.1rem}.system-node b{font-size:.68rem}.system-node span{font-size:.53rem}.system-node small{font-size:.43rem}.system-link{padding:.08rem;font-size:.45rem}.system-foot{margin-top:.3rem;padding-top:.3rem;font-size:.42rem}.brief-footer{font-size:.42rem}.brief-footer span:last-child{display:none}}
@@media(max-height:700px) and (min-width:621px){.brief-message h1{font-size:clamp(2rem,4.4vw,4rem);margin:.4rem 0}.brief-lede{line-height:1.35;margin:.35rem 0}.brief-claim{margin-top:.4rem;padding:.5rem .65rem}.brief-steps{margin-top:.5rem}.brief-actions{margin-top:.5rem}.brief-system{padding:.55rem}.system-node{padding:.3rem .5rem}.system-link{padding:.08rem}.brief-footer{font-size:.45rem}}
</style>

@code {
    private int _stage;

    private void SetStage(int stage) => _stage = Math.Clamp(stage, 0, 3);

    private void RequestBriefing()
    {
        var subject = Uri.EscapeDataString("Technical development briefing — The Singularity Workshop");
        var body = Uri.EscapeDataString("Hello,\n\nI'd like to discuss The Singularity Workshop's current development and a potential technical or institutional fit.\n\nOrganization / program:\nProblem or mission area:\nExisting systems / technical constraints:\nEvidence or validation required:\nDesired next step:\n\nThank you.");
        Navigation.NavigateTo($"mailto:thesingularityworkshop@gmail.com?subject={subject}&body={body}");
    }
}
